    "chunk_size_bytes": 1955,
    "chunk_text": "Deep Tec Engineering expands to uplift rural Sri Lanka through sustainable water and solar solutions\n\nDeep Tec Engineering Ltd., a pioneering force in sustainable water solutions, is reaffirming its commitment to transforming rural communities through innovative and environmentally conscious technologies.\n\nToday, Deep Tec holds an industry-leading 28% market share in solar water pumps, underscoring its technical excellence and strong customer trust. The company also delivers nearly $ 2 million worth of solar water pump projects annually in collaboration with international development agencies, including the United Nations, the World Bank, and other global partners.\n\nThese long-standing collaborations highlight the company\u2019s proven capability, transparency, and alignment with international sustainability and community-development priorities.\n\nOver the past decade, the company has expanded its footprint across the island, enabling thousands of families and farmers to access life-changing water resources for drinking, agriculture, and livelihood development. Deep Tec\u2019s unique model integrates advanced solar power technologies to ensure that rural water systems operate efficiently, affordably, and without dependence on fossil fuels or grid electricity. This commitment to sustainability has placed the company at the forefront of Sri Lanka\u2019s green engineering movement.\n\nDeep Tec\u2019s success is driven by the leadership and vision of its Managing Director, Thilina Hettiarachchi, whose passion for uplifting rural Sri Lanka has shaped the company\u2019s culture and mission. Hettiarachchi has been widely recognised for his contribution to social engineering and rural development. Most recently, he was named Best Entrepreneur of the Year 2025 at the Iconic Awards 2025, an accolade that reflects his dedication to expanding access to water, empowering farming communities, and championing renewable energy adoption across the country."
